    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Symbotic Inc. describes itself as a provider of end-to-end warehouse automation solutions for retailers and distributors. Its website says the company's Symbotic Solutions and Symbotic Systems are complete, turnkey-ready automation offerings that increase facility capacity through dense storage, maximize throughput, and create supply chain efficiency gains with AI-enhanced software. The company states its systems can handle palletized goods, small quantity fulfillment, and omnichannel operations, with goods from 1 lb (0.5 kg) and 2 x 6.4 x 5 in (5.1 x 16.3 x 12.7 cm) up to 60 lb (27.2 kg) and 36 x 24 x 16.2 in (91.4 x 61 x 41.2 cm), including cold chain options.\n\nThe company positions itself as a software and key robotic innovator for each solution, rather than a typical integrator limited by technology partnerships. It describes its purpose as getting the right goods to people who need them, when they need them, and says it is innovating through robotics and AI for material access.\n\nSymbotic Inc. is a public company headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts, trading under the ticker SYM with SEC CIK 0001837240. The company has 191 Massachusetts law exposure entries and no recorded litigation cases. No MCP servers are listed.",
